It is Friday after work.
I am standing in a small bakery near the office.
I am buying a dessert for Nele.
The baker smiles at me.
"What would you like?" he asks.
"I will take this small fruit tart, please," I say.
I explain to him that I am buying the tart for a friend.
"That is a nice idea," he answers.
"That comes to eight euros fifty."
I give him a ten-euro note.
He gives me the change and the receipt.
Then he packs the tart into a light cardboard box.
"I thank you," I say and take the box carefully.
I look at my backpack.
I know that the tart will get ruined in the backpack.
So I do not pack it away.
I will carry the box completely flat in my hands.
Like this, I am now walking to the U-Bahn.
